Creates a new preauthkey

Usage: headscale preauthkeys create [OPTIONS]

Options:
  -c, --config <CONFIG>          config file (default is /etc/headscale/config.yaml) [env: HEADSCALE_CONFIG=]
  -u, --user <USER>              User identifier (ID)
      --reusable                 Make the preauthkey reusable
      --ephemeral                Preauthkey for ephemeral nodes
      --tags <TAGS>              Tags to automatically assign to node
  -e, --expiration <EXPIRES_IN>  Human-readable expiration of the key (e.g. 30m, 24h) [default: 1h]
  -o, --output <OUTPUT>          Output format. Empty for human-readable, 'json', 'json-line' or 'yaml'
      --force                    Disable prompts and forces the execution
  -h, --help                     Print help
